      <Text>SPEAKER 1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>one in m butterfly is named. It's named song. But I don't know if I don't think that's the name in, I think in Puccini, she's just butterfly, oh, but in, but in m butterfly, she is Song lilling, I think, Well, whoever.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SPEAKER 2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I can't remember that name, but the Madame Butterfly, Puccini character. Then there's Kim, and then there's so it's first, just the two of them in, like, the</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>UNKNOWN SPEAKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>afterlife, well, first, and just one of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SPEAKER 2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh yeah, first. And they just have to keep reliving their story over and over, of like, having a baby and then killing and they're like, living their life, like, Hold on, I have to have a baby now and then, like, oh, not to kill myself. And then they discover and then Kim comes along and is doing the same thing. And then they bring in the woman that was, like, made tabloids for like, they said that she was, like, thought the Fargo story was real, and</Text>
